course: dictionary
lesson: 1240
title: Bumpy: rough ground, rough ride, rough start
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Bumpy usually means not smooth. A bumpy road has lumps and holes, so a car shakes as it goes over it. Look at the words around the word to check. In «the bumpy back of the beetle», bumpy tells you the back has lumps, not that it is wet or cold.
explain: Bumpy can also describe a ride. «Turbulence is bumpy air, like waves in the sky» means the plane is shaken up and down, like a boat on rough water. The clue is the word air, because air cannot have lumps you can feel on your feet.
explain: Bumpy can also describe a hard start, such as «a bumpy start». Test it by swapping in another word. A rough start still makes sense, so bumpy means rough or full of problems here.
fact: Bumpy means not smooth, with lumps and holes.
fact: Bumpy air is called turbulence, and it can shake a plane with no warning.
fact: Bumpy can describe a surface, a ride, or a hard start.
fact: Bumpy surfaces have more friction than smooth ones, so toy cars slow down faster on them.
fact: The bumpy soles of your shoes grip the ground, which helps you walk and stop.
exercise: «A warthog's warts are thick bumpy pads that protect its face in fights.» What does bumpy mean here? | Smooth and shiny | Soft and warm | *Covered in lumps and bumps | Very loud
exercise: «The plane was bumpy because of strong wind.» What does bumpy describe? | A plane that is painted red | A plane with a broken wing | *A ride where you are shaken up and down | A very smooth, quiet flight
exercise: Leo says «a bumpy start» means a fun, easy start. What does it really mean? | Warm and tasty | *Hard and full of problems | Fun and easy | Quick and smooth
test: Which word means about the same as bumpy when a road has lumps and holes? | *Lumpy | Shiny | Warm | Silent
test: Why do toy cars slow down faster on bumpy surfaces? | Bumpy surfaces are always wet | *Bumpy surfaces have more friction than smooth ones | Toy cars get heavier on bumpy ground | Bumpy surfaces make toy cars float
exam: In «a bumpy road ahead», what does bumpy mean? | *Full of hard things to get through | Covered in soft grass | Covered in snow | Very bright and shiny
